<title>FRANCE: France's Jospin would discuss euro with Germany.</title>
<headline>France's Jospin would discuss euro with Germany.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Socialist leader Lionel Jospin said on Tuesday he would negotiate with Germany over the starting date for the euro if he came to power in France.</p>
<p>Asked in a television interview if he favoured a delay of the euro, he said: &quot;If we were in power in June, we would have almost a year to make proposals to our partners, particularly to the Germans, on these questions.&quot;</p>
<p>Jospin said on Sunday that he would not adopt new austerity measures because of the high unemployment rate.</p>
<p>President Jacques Chirac on Monday announced an early parliamentary election to be held in two rounds on May 25 and June 1.</p>
</text>
